@* Louis: routing, the ring that was "accuracy" first, kept under its own name: the conversations Puls sent where they
   should go (green) and where they shouldn't (red), the share in its middle. *@
<RingChart Topic="routing" Title="Routing per mode" Legend="ExplorerLegends.Routing">
    @foreach (var (m, i) in Tree.Columns)
    {
        <ModeDonut I="i" Who="@ModeNames.Who(m)" Figure="ModeRings.Routing(m)" />
    }
</RingChart>

@* Louis: accuracy is the answer, not the routing ("this is not true" of a 100 % ring over a run that priced nothing).
   Where the check lists ingredients (the cook check): each priced with its source (green), guessed without one
   (orange) or unknown (red), the share sourced in its middle, and the meals that came without a list under it. A
   check without ingredients has routing as its accuracy, so no second ring. *@
@if (Tree.Modes.Any(m => ExplorerScores.Accuracy(m) is not null))
{
    <RingChart Topic="accuracy" Title="Accuracy per mode" Legend="ExplorerLegends.Accuracy">
        @foreach (var (m, i) in Tree.Columns)
        {
            <ModeDonut I="i" Who="@ModeNames.Who(m)" Figure="ModeRings.Accuracy(m)">
                @if (ExplorerScores.Unlisted(m) is > 0 and var none) { <small class="muted">@none @(none == 1 ? "meal" : "meals") without a list</small> }
            </ModeDonut>
        }
    </RingChart>
}
